      "id": 1,
      "text": "Milledgeville grew around a gristmill built in 1834, giving the village its name.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Milledgeville%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1886, town leaders raised $16,000 to bring the Chicago, Burlington and Quincy railroad through Milledgeville, opening the town to the world.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
